| Mixed for !Freeciv: run by !Run when the client is the "mixed" program
| FreecivSDL. UnixLib, libstdc++ and Freeciv's own libraries are linked
| into it; SDL 2, EGL and OSMesa are shared libraries from riscos-mesa's
| !MesaLibs, which !SharedLibs's loader (ld-riscos/so/2) loads.

| Boot !SharedLibs, then !MesaLibs (which puts ld-riscos/so/2 into
| !SharedLibs if it isn't there), if the Filer hasn't seen them yet.
If "<SharedLibs$Dir>" = "" Then IfThere Boot:Resources.!SharedLibs.!Boot Then Run Boot:Resources.!SharedLibs.!Boot
If "<MesaLibs$Dir>" = "" Then IfThere Boot:Resources.!MesaLibs.!Boot Then Run Boot:Resources.!MesaLibs.!Boot
If "<SharedLibs$Dir>" = "" Then Error Freeciv needs !SharedLibs (from PackMan) in !Boot.Resources.
If "<MesaLibs$Dir>" = "" Then Error Freeciv needs !MesaLibs 20.3.5-23 or later in !Boot.Resources. It's in riscos-mesa-MesaLibs-20.3.5-23.zip from github.com/adyoull/riscos-mesa/releases. Restart the computer after installing it.
Unset Freeciv$SO2
IfThere SharedLibs:lib.ld-riscos-eabihf/so Then Set Freeciv$SO2 1
If "<Freeciv$SO2>" = "" Then Error The !SharedLibs booted has no ld-riscos/so/2: Freeciv needs a newer one (GCCSDK 8 or later) in !Boot.Resources.
Unset Freeciv$SO2

| Where the loader finds the libraries: SOManager reads <program>$LD$Env.
Set FreecivSDL$LD$Env "LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/MesaLibs:"
